# Q: does the computer opponent build a defensive line, put it on ground worth standing on, and
#    keep its radar on the air while it does?
#
#   MiVic.Game.exe --probe tools/probe/ai-line.probe --probe-out artifacts/probe/ai-line.txt
#
# The default skirmish, unmodified, with nobody playing team 0: three bases on the standard map and
# teams 1 and 2 run by AiSystem. Nothing in this script places a building or orders a unit — every
# structure below is one the AI decided to raise, on a site the AI chose, judged by the same rule a
# player's click is judged by. That is the question: `structures` says what it built and where,
# `power` says whether it can still run it, `attributes` says what the ground it chose is worth,
# `range` says whether the radar gave the guns the reach they were bought for, and `unit` says
# whether an emplacement is firing on its own.
#
# The line is expected in this order: a Πυροβολείo from about tick 40 (120 ticks of work for the
# Κινέζοι), then the Σταθμός Ραντάρ that gives it its 200 m, then a second gun, then the
# Αντιαεροπορικό Πυροβολείο once the era that builds aircraft has been researched. The slots are this
# run's own and are stable because a probe is deterministic: guns 510 and 513 and the radar 511 are
# the three the line raises first, and the anti-aircraft emplacement, which comes later and lands in
# whichever slot a casualty has freed by then, is 190. It used to be 427: the AI now spends on the
# generation and the yards that lift a command ceiling its opening army is over, so more structures
# and more material move through the world before that emplacement is ordered, and the slot it lands
# in moved with them. See `capacity.probe` for that half of the AI's loop.

# --- what the AI started with ------------------------------------------------------------------
tick 2
structures 1
power 1

# --- the decision, three seconds in -----------------------------------------------------------------
# Three building sites for team 1 and two for team 2, raised within three decisions of the match
# starting, none of them at an offset from anything: a gun, the radar that will give it its reach,
# and a second gun. Every one of them is rising on a cell the AI picked out of the ground around its
# base. Team 2's line does not survive the match — the Κινέζοι army takes its base apart — which is
# what a real match looks like and why team 1 is the one read further down.
tick 60
structures 1
structures 2
power 1
power 2

# --- half a minute in: the line ----------------------------------------------------------------
tick 500
structures 1
structures 2
power 1
power 2

# --- the ground the AI chose ---------------------------------------------------------------------
# The two Πυροβολεία, the cells they stand on, and — for comparison — the ground under the
# headquarters they were bought to defend. `cover foot` is how much of a shot aimed at the building
# lands: 1000 ‰ is no cover at all. Both guns are standing in closed woodland in a valley, which is
# 540 ‰ and 563 ‰, and the headquarters' own cell is 927 ‰. That difference is the whole of what the
# site search maximised, and it is the same number the combat system scales every hit on them by.
attributes 42.2 4.7
attributes 4.7 -61
attributes 145.3 -98.5

# --- the radar, and what it is worth to the gun --------------------------------------------------
# A Πυροβολείο sees 170 m and shoots 200, so its reach is 170 until a powered radar covers the ground
# both ends of the shot stand on — and the whole 200 once one does.
range 510
range 511

# --- the gun firing with nobody having ordered it -------------------------------------------------
# `order automatic` is the client reading the simulation: the emplacement picked that target itself.
# And the target is 193 m away, which is past the 170 m this gun can see on its own — the shot is the
# radar's, as much as the gun's.
unit 510
unit 513
events 12

# --- and a minute in, with the anti-aircraft emplacement up -------------------------------------
tick 600
structures 1
power 1
range 190

# --- the ledger after all of it, which is the failure mode this feature can create ---------------
# Generation against load, and the dish still on the air: an AI that raises a radar its grid cannot
# run has made itself worse than one that never built it, because detection is what the ledger sheds
# first.
tick 600
power 1
power 2
structures 1

# --- the ledger of measurements -------------------------------------------------------------------
# Written down as the numbers they were read as, so that the day the AI stops building a line — or
# starts shedding the radar it built — this script fails instead of quietly reporting something else.
expect "the gun's own eyes" 170.0 170.0 0
expect "the gun's gun" 200.0 200.0 0
expect "the reach the radar gives it" 200.0 200.0 0
expect "the radar covers" 260.0 260.0 0
expect "the anti-aircraft emplacement reaches" 180.0 180.0 0
expect "gun emplacements raised" 2 2 0
expect "radar stations raised" 1 1 0
expect "anti-aircraft emplacements raised" 1 1 0
expect "and the other AI team raised its own gun" 1 1 0
expect "and its own radar" 1 1 0
expect "generation" 16 16 0
expect "load" 11 11 0
expect "radars dark" 0 0 0
expect "the cover the first gun stands in, in permille" 540 540 0
expect "the cover the second gun stands in, in permille" 563 563 0
